    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with a clear focal point in **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (82.13), who headlines our lineup. His elite speed profile coupled with the matchup against Lowder provides the highest upside for our scarcity-driven strategy; the combination of a positive park factor and a slow-delivering pitcher creates a high-probability environment for stolen bases. Similarly, **Christian Yelich** (74.33) and **Yordan Alvarez** (74.02) project as top-tier starts. **Christian Yelich** leverages a significant platoon advantage against Brandon Young in a favorable park, while **Yordan Alvarez** remains a core play despite the negative platoon split because his raw talent and xwOBA remain too elite to fade, even against a tough lefty in Mart\u00edn P\u00e9rez.\n\nEfficiency dictates our remaining slots, where **Junior Caminero** (64.57) and **Trea Turner** (63.37) provide steady production. We are navigating significant risk at the corners: **Kazuma Okamoto** (40.41) faces the formidable Jacob deGrom, whose sub-3.00 xERA suppresses **Kazuma Okamoto**\u2019s ceiling significantly. Consequently, the optimizer had to weigh tough decisions on the bench. **Chase Meidroth** (48.59) was the most difficult exclusion; he offered more stability than **Christian Encarnacion-Strand** (48.89), but the latter\u2019s extreme park boost against Jacob Misiorowski ultimately pushed him into the UTIL slot. We must remain cautious of the \"Lineup Pending\" status for players like **Gary Sanchez**, **Dillon Dingler**, **Colt Keith**, **Josh Smith**, **Lars Nootbaar**, and **Christian Encarnacion-Strand**, as any unexpected defensive substitutions or late rest days will require immediate recalibration of our game caps. **Caleb Durbin**, **Carson Benge**, **Casey Schmitt**, **Luis Pena**, **Jacob Gonzalez**, and **Hector Rodriguez** remain on standby should injury or late-scratches necessitate a pivot.",
